<launch>
  <!-- =====================================================================
       transbot_dashboard.launch — rosbridge ONLY.

       Phase 1 discovery (FINDINGS.md) showed the factory stack autostarts
       at boot with everything else the dashboard needs:
         - transbot_driver.py (owns all hardware)
         - web_video_server on :8080 (camera MJPEG, topic /image)
       So the only missing piece is the WebSocket bridge. Do NOT include
       bringup.launch here — a second driver instance collides with the
       factory one and both die.

       Deployed to ~/transbot_dashboard/ on the Jetson in Phase 2, after
       ros-melodic-rosbridge-suite is installed (explicit go-ahead required).
       ===================================================================== -->

  <include file="$(find rosbridge_server)/launch/rosbridge_websocket.launch">
    <arg name="port" value="9090" />
  </include>
</launch>
